<title>AUSTRIA: IRAN SAYS HOPES TO FINALISE SOUTH PARS DEAL SOON.</title>
<headline>IRAN SAYS HOPES TO FINALISE SOUTH PARS DEAL SOON.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iranian Oil Minister Gholamreza Aghazadeh on Thursday said he hopes within two months to have finalised a deal with a western oil company to develop Iran's huge South Pars gas field.</p>
<p>&quot;I hope in the near future, in a maximum of two months, we will sign an agreement,&quot; the minister told a news briefing.</p>
<p>He said Total SA and Royal Dutch/Shell Group were still both in the running for the project which is for a second and third phase development of the field.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 713 2002</p>
</text>
